<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       Class manuals turn up in trade, occasionally.

       Until now the only ways into a class were finding a manual in loot
       or being taught by a companion, which left a party that missed both
       with no route at all. A merchant who deals in books is a third one -
       deliberately unreliable and expensive, so it supplements the hunt
       rather than replacing it.

       StockGenerator_Category with countRange 0~1 and a low
       thingDefCountRange means most visits carry nothing, and a visit that
       does carries one manual of whichever kind the roll gave.

       Applied to the traders who would plausibly have books: the exotic
       caravans, the shaman/war merchants of the tribal circuit, and
       outlander settlements. Not bulk goods, not pirates.
       ================================================================== -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/TraderKindDef[
        defName="Caravan_Outlander_Exotic" or
        defName="Caravan_Neolithic_ShamanMerchant" or
        defName="Caravan_Neolithic_WarMerchant" or
        defName="Base_Outlander_Standard" or
        defName="Base_Neolithic_Standard" or
        defName="Visitor_Outlander_Standard"
      ]/stockGenerators</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="StockGenerator_Category">
        <categoryDef>TSC_ClassBooks</categoryDef>
        <thingDefCountRange>0~1</thingDefCountRange>
        <countRange>1~1</countRange>
        <price>Expensive</price>
      </li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
